  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=9.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ 9(0)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions.\nSo, there are no $y$-intercepts.",
